  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Let $V$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices with real entries and determinant $0.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\nI. The zero-matrix $[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $V.$\n\nII. Scalar multiplication of matrices in $V$ is associative.\n\nIII. For any $A,B\\in V$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (A+B)=\\alpha A+\\alpha B.$",
